The Opportunity:
The Sr. Manager, Customer & Supplier Communications​ is responsible for defining and executing audience-specific communications strategy across multiple business segments and regions to support business objectives, strengthen stakeholder engagement, and help build and protect the company’s brands. This role will establish and enhance communications best practices, operating rhythms, and governance within the assigned audience scope while partnering with business leaders to enable sales growth through traditional and digital communications channels.
The Sr. Manager will shape communications direction for the assigned audience beyond program execution, including strategy development, senior leadership positioning, storytelling, message consistency, channel governance, quality control, and measurement. The role will support transformation, culture, commercial, and change initiatives with measurable communications outcomes across relevant functions or business units, while aligning with enterprise communications standards and broader organizational priorities.
The role will report to the Head of VWR Communications and serve as the primary communications leader for the assigned audience, with accountability for communications strategy and outcomes across multiple regions and stakeholder groups within that scope.
How you will thrive and create an impact

• Advise and support senior leaders on audience-specific communications strategy, strategic messaging, channels, delivery approach, and execution of key initiatives across multiple regions;

• Develop and implement communications strategies, plans, governance, and cadence aligned to business objectives for the assigned audience, business segments, and regional stakeholder groups;

• Drive the strategic narrative using best practices, audience insights, and the right communications channels to reach targeted associate, customer, supplier, or commercial stakeholder segments and facilitate leadership engagement as needed;

• Ensure consistency and continuity of messaging, standards, approvals, and program support across the assigned audience and key stakeholders;

• Optimize and maintain communications platforms, tools, and operating frameworks to advance new ways to tell the organization’s story, strengthen engagement, and support culture or commercial change within the assigned scope;

• Align outreach with strategic business and functional goals, lead the evolution or expansion of existing communications programs, and shape communications direction beyond day-to-day program execution;

• Drive two-way dialogue and engagement to amplify key messages and understanding of our brand

• Plan, manage, and communicate change, transformation, culture, or commercial initiatives in a fast-changing, highly dynamic environment with measurable communications impact;

• Align with Corporate External and Internal Communication strategies, policies, standards, and tactics that effectively communicate Avantor ’s culture, vision, and goals in support of growth initiatives;

• Provide proactive counsel to key internal stakeholders on communications strategies and programs that advance commercial, customer, supplier, associate, or business objectives within the assigned audience scope;

• Collaborate with functional team members, corporate and business communications partners, and regional stakeholders to develop integrated programming as needed;

• Define, drive, and refine KPIs, metrics, and reporting mechanisms to measure communications outcomes, assess program performance, and enable continuous improvement;

• Support issues/crisis communications as needed

• Oversee agency partners when appropriate

• Lead and ensure appropriate communications processes, governance, and approval standards are followed, including final approvals from subject matter experts, project owners, compliance, and legal partners;

• Measure, track, and analyze overall program effectiveness to determine ROI,

Civil Engineer - Offshore and Cable Projects
Who we are
Elia Grid International (EGI) is a global power systems consultancy driving innovation and excellence across the global energy sector. Building on the expertise of Elia Group (Belgium) and 50Hertz (Germany) ,EGI delivers strategic, technical, and regulatory advisory services to tackle complex challenges of the energy transition.
With offices in Belgium, Germany, the UAE, Saudi Arabia, Malaysia, Canada, and the USA, EGI partners with clients across the globe to deliver high-impact projects in power system planning, smart grids design & digitalization, asset management, HVDC, FACTS, and renewable integration.
As we continue to scale up and expand internationally, our ambition is to become a global leader in power systems consultancy, helping build resilient and sustainable energy systems worldwide.
Your function
We are looking for an experienced Civil Engineer with strong experience in civil aspects of HV transmission projects, more specific civil related cable installation topics and onshore construction of substations/converter stations. .
You would report to the Senior Project Engineer on the project.
Typical activities involve (but are not limited to):

• Define plant-specific requirements for the HVDC converter station and cable systems, especially civil engineering topics.

• Evaluate sites from a civil engineering perspective in terms of feasibility and technical challenges

• Evaluate and provide input to cable route feasibility from the civil engineering perspective (e.g. crossings, HDD, access restrictions…)

• Control the entire technical implementation process, from drafting tender documents to awarding contracts.

• Draw up comparisons of technical and economic alternatives and doing preparatory work for cost-intensive investment decisions.

Your profile

• Diploma or master's degree in civil engineering;

• Several years of experience within infrastructure projects as a civil design & engineer, consulting engineer or project manager for a contractor, engineering/consulting company and/or employer;

• Understanding of civil engineering requirements of power infrastructure projects especially outdoor HV substation design, HVDC converter stations, , buildings, roads, trenches and crossings (HDD), steel structures, and control buildings;

• Experiences in civil works, planning, design, tendering. Experience from executing is a plus.;

• Capable to determine the work scope for green field projects;

• Experiences and capability to work in a team of engineers to execute complex transmission projects in Germany ;

• Experience in project implementation according to the HOAI;

• Fluent in English;

• Specific experience and knowledge of landfall civil works (e.g. cable landing HDD) is an asset

What we offer

• Permanent contract or freelance position;

• Attractive salary package and an extensive array of fringe benefits;

• Exciting, professional and international environment in a fast-growing company;

• Unique training, personal development and growth opportunities;

At EGI, we value diversity and inclusion. We are firmly committed to promoting gender equality in all aspects of our organization, from recruitment to professional development. We believe that diverse teams are more creative, innovative, and high-performing. Join us to contribute to an environment where everyone has equal opportunities for growth and fulfilment.
Choose EGI and help us guide the worldwide power sector into a future of clean and sustainable energy, smarter and more flexible grids, decentralized production and HVDC systems that span across seas and land to interconnect countries, regions, and different energy markets for the benefit of generations to come.
Location
Remote working.
Travel required to the project sites and occasionally for project team meetings.
